846 (2025-11-24) · high 9,115 (2026-06-22)</div>\n<div class=\"obp-row\">vs 1Y average -20.4% · 1W -7.9% · 1M -12.0%</div>\n<div class=\"obp-note\">Korea&#x27;s main stock market index (excluding dividends) · 2026-11-20 close</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n<div id=\"ondo-board-data\" hidden data-json=\"{&quot;updated&quot;: &quot;2026-11-22 11:35 KST&quot;, &quot;items&quot;: [{&quot;t&quot;: &quot;KRW=X&quot;, &quot;name&quot;: &quot;KRW per USD&quot;, &quot;unit&quot;: &quot;KRW&quot;, &quot;value&quot;: &quot;1,334.8&quot;, &quot;pos&quot;: 6, &quot;as_of&quot;: &quot;2026-11-20&quot;}, {&quot;t&quot;: &quot;^TNX&quot;, &quot;name&quot;: &quot;US 10-year Treasury yield&quot;, &quot;unit&quot;: &quot;%&quot;, &quot;value&quot;: &quot;4.912&quot;, &quot;pos&quot;: 70, &quot;as_of&quot;: &quot;2026-11-20&quot;}, {&quot;t&quot;: &quot;^VIX&quot;, &quot;name&quot;: &quot;Volatility index (VIX)&quot;, &quot;unit&quot;: &quot;&quot;, &quot;value&quot;: &quot;35.89&quot;, &quot;pos&quot;: 100, &quot;as_of&quot;: &quot;2026-11-20&quot;}, {&quot;t&quot;: &quot;BZ=F&quot;, &quot;name&quot;: &quot;Brent crude&quot;, &quot;unit&quot;: &quot;USD/bbl&quot;, &quot;value&quot;: &quot;92.57&quot;, &quot;pos&quot;: 57, &quot;as_of&quot;: &quot;2026-11-20&quot;}, {&quot;t&quot;: &quot;GC=F&quot;, &quot;name&quot;: &quot;Gold&quot;, &quot;unit&quot;: &quot;USD/oz&quot;, &quot;value&quot;: &quot;3,515.4&quot;, &quot;pos&quot;: 0, &quot;as_of&quot;: &quot;2026-11-20&quot;}, {&quot;t&quot;: &quot;^GSPC&quot;, &quot;name&quot;: &quot;S&amp;P 500&quot;, &quot;unit&quot;: &quot;&quot;, &quot;value&quot;: &quot;6,910&quot;, &quot;pos&quot;: 38, &quot;as_of&quot;: &quot;2026-11-20&quot;}, {&quot;t&quot;: &quot;^KS11&quot;, &quot;name&quot;: &quot;KOSPI&quot;, &quot;unit&quot;: &quot;&quot;, &quot;value&quot;: &quot;4,870&quot;, &quot;pos&quot;: 19, &quot;as_of&quot;: &quot;2026-11-20&quot;}]}\"></div>\n<div class=\"obp-sec\">\n<h3><span>HOW TO READ</span>Reading the temperature</h3>\n<p>The temperature only means &#8220;where the current value sits within the past year&#8217;s range&#8221;. 100° does not mean it cannot go higher, and 0° does not mean it has hit bottom. It is a quick way to tell, when you see the same number in the news, whether it is high or low by the standard of the past year.</p>\n</div>\n<div class=\"obp-sec\">\n<h3><span>METHOD</span>How it is calculated</h3>\n<p>Temperature = (current value − 1-year low) ÷ (1-year high − 1-year low) × 100. Versus 1-year average = current value ÷ average of daily closes over the past year − 1. 1-week and 1-month changes compare with the close 5 and 21 trading days earlier. Oil and gold use front-month futures, so values can jump when the contract rolls. Indices are price-only, excluding dividends. Indicators whose data could not be fetched are left out that day. The 20 cells split 0°–100° into steps of about 5°. The large bar and the temperature use the 1-year range; the small bars (3Y·5Y) apply the same calculation to the past 3 and 5 years &#8211; a longer period means a wider range, so the same value can show a different temperature.</p>\n<p>This page is not investment advice (<a href=\"/en/disclaimer-en/\">Disclaimer</a>).</p>\n</div>\n</div>\n",
